# RULE BEFORE PLAN AND CODE

Cursor-only rule. It adds one thing `AGENTS.md` does not: a plan-and-approve gate before any source code is written. Everything else (session, `.context`, GitNexus, docs routing, reuse, quality gates, subagent limits, documentation sync) is defined in `AGENTS.md` and its skills, which always win over this file.

## 1. Gate: plan first, code after approval

* For any task that changes source code, do not write or edit source code until the user has explicitly approved the plan (for example "Approved", "Proceed", or `/opsx:apply`).
* Allowed before approval: reading files, GitNexus analysis, creating or updating documentation, OpenSpec artifacts, and the plan itself.
* If the user's request already contains explicit approval, say so in one line and continue.

## 2. Protected files

* Never edit `AGENTS-example.md`, `CLAUDE-example.md`, or the read-only specs `sample_chuc_nang.md`, `sample_curl_api.md`, `sample_modules.md`, `sample_sql_full.md` (when present).
* If a task needs a change to one of them, stop and report.

## 3. Task analysis

Before planning, state: objective, constraints, expected outcome, affected modules, related pages or components, APIs involved, data-flow impact, what must not be touched, risks and edge cases. Follow the documentation routing in `AGENTS.md` (`Repository specifics`) instead of re-discovering the repository; check the shared-assets file before proposing any new utility, type, or helper, and reuse what exists.

## 4. The plan

Record it in `docs/ALL-SPRINTS.md` (a row in `In progress` with item, owner, OpenSpec change) or in the OpenSpec change (`proposal.md`, `design.md`, `tasks.md`); never in a new file at the repository root. It must contain:

* Discovery summary and related features
* Reusability strategy: existing assets to reuse, new reusable assets and why
* Files to add, modify, delete (exact paths, reason, estimated lines, logic description)
* Risks, edge cases, and how it will be verified

Then reply: "The implementation plan has been recorded in <place>. Please review and provide explicit approval (e.g., 'Approved', 'Proceed') before I begin coding." and stop.

## 5. Execution

* Follow the approved plan and the existing architecture; make no assumptions.
* Extract reusable logic into the correct shared folder; never put all utilities in one module and never duplicate reusable logic.
* Update the documentation entries that changed (not chat-only summaries), including the shared-assets file when reusable logic is created or modified.
* Run the quality gate named in `AGENTS.md`, then request a review of the diff.

## 6. Failure handling

Stop immediately, explain clearly, do not guess, and do not partially implement.
